 "wiki": {
  "title": "Common snipe",
  "extract": "The common snipe is a small, stocky wader native to the Old World, where it breeds in marshes, bogs, tundra and wet meadows. It is usually shy and well-camouflaged, foraging in soft mud mainly for insects and earthworms but also some plant material. During courtship, males perform a \"winnowing\" display; flying high in circles and then taking shallow dives to produce a \"drumming\" sound by vibrating the tail feathers.",
